        <item>
            <title>1.0.0</title>
            <pubDate>Tue, 10 Nov 2026 14:19:46 -0700</pubDate>
            <sparkle:channel>beta</sparkle:channel>
            <sparkle:version>20261110.1419</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>1.0.0</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>15.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <description><![CDATA[<!doctype html><meta charset="utf-8"><style>body{font:13px -apple-system,sans-serif;margin:12px}h1,h2{font-size:15px}</style><h2>Kaiju 1.0.0 RC2</h2>
<ul>
<li><b>Import single set list slots:</b> in <b>Import from another PCG › Set Lists</b>, the eye button (or right-click › <b>Show Slots…</b>) shows the set list as on the KRONOS, in pages of 16 slots with their colors; click the slots to bring and only those slots and their sounds come along. <b>Copy its EQ</b> (on unless you uncheck it) brings the set list's EQ too. In step 2 the slots can go to an empty set list, in the same numbers, or into the empty slots of one of your set lists in use (<b>In use — add to its empty slots</b>), which keeps its name and slots (and its EQ, if Copy its EQ is unchecked).
</li>
<li><b>Double-click a .PCG to open it in Kaiju:</b> Kaiju now opens .PCG files and .KSC sample banks from Finder (or dropped on its Dock icon). If another app opens them, <b>Settings › Files › Make Kaiju the Default</b>.
</li>
<li><b>Renamed programs are recognized:</b> importing a song whose combi this PCG already has (e.g. a single that is also in the full pack) no longer copies it again just because one of its programs was renamed in the pack: what a combi plays is compared by sound, not by name.
</li>
<li><b>Continue reopens your whole session:</b> on the welcome screen, the Continue card opens every file you had open last time, not just the last one.
</li>
<li><b>"Discard Changes"</b> is the new name of the Discard button.
</li>
<li><b>Back up with Save PCG:</b> Kaiju now suggests <b>Disk › Save › Save PCG</b> (not Save All, which also writes empty KGE and SNG files and duplicates sample data).
</li>
<li><b>The version shows RC2</b> in the status bar, About and What's New.
</li>
<li>Support is now at <b>support@kaijueditor.com</b>.
</li></ul>]]></description>
