        <item>
            <title>0.9.22</title>
            <pubDate>Fri, 06 Nov 2026 10:26:51 -0700</pubDate>
            <sparkle:channel>beta</sparkle:channel>
            <sparkle:version>20261106.1025</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>0.9.22</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>15.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <description><![CDATA[<!doctype html><meta charset="utf-8"><style>body{font:13px -apple-system,sans-serif;margin:12px}h1,h2{font-size:15px}</style><h2>Kaiju 0.9.22 beta</h2>
<ul>
<li><b>Initialized banks read as empty:</b> "Init" programs and combis that are identical to several others count as empty, even when the KRONOS that initialized them (another OS version) filled a parameter differently. A bank initialized on the keyboard no longer shows 128 used. A single edited "Init" still counts as used.
</li>
<li><b>Sort part of a set list:</b> select several slots, right-click › <b>Sort N slots</b> › by name A→Z or Z→A. Only those slots are sorted, among their own positions; the rest of the set list stays put.
</li>
<li><b>Dual View / Single View:</b> the button to see two set lists side by side is now called <b>Dual View</b> (and <b>Single View</b> to go back).
</li>
<li><b>Color for several slots:</b> with several slots selected, the color is chosen from the same named grid as for one slot (Default, Charcoal, Brick…).
</li>
<li><b>New sounds marked:</b> combis and programs you paste or import show a small <b>NEW</b> tag and a colored bar, and their bank a dot, until you close the PCG, so they're easy to find.
</li>
<li><b>⌘C ⌘X ⌘V ⌘A and Delete in Programs and Combis</b> work reliably (they sometimes beeped).
</li></ul>]]></description>
